ices and determinants in the MS Word documents using native Word equation formatting. (Status: **COMPLETED**)\n\n---\n\n### 2. User Knowledge\n- **Formatting Guidelines:**\n  - File format: Word (`.docx`) required. (PDFs not accepted).\n  - Typography: Times New Roman, 12 pt, Automatic Black font.\n  - Page layout: A4, Portrait orientation, Narrow margins (1.27 cm / 0.5 in), Single paragraph spacing.\n  - No box frames to separate questions.\n  - Page numbering & proper section headers (`SECTION A`, `SECTION B`, etc.).\n- **Chapter-wise Mark Weightage (Total: 80 Marks):**\n  - Relations & Functions: 8 Marks\n  - Inverse Trigonometric Functions: 8 Marks\n  - Matrices: 10 Marks\n  - Determinants: 10 Marks\n  - Continuity & Differentiability: 14 Marks\n  - Application of Derivatives: 14 Marks\n  - Integrals: 16 Marks\n- **Deleted Syllabus (Strict NCERT Rationalized Syllabus Compliance):**\n  - Relations & Functions: Composition of functions, invertible functions, binary operations.\n  - Inverse Trig Functions: Elementary properties/identities (e.g. $\\tan^{-1} a + \\tan^{-1} b$, $2\\tan^{-1} x$).\n  - Matrices: Elementary row/column transformations.\n  - Determinants: Proof-based properties of determinants.\n  - Continuity & Differentiability: Rolle's and Lagrange's Mean Value Theorems.\n  - Application of Derivatives: Tangents and Normals, Approximations.\n  - Integrals: Definite integral as limit of a sum.\n- **User Verbatim Requests:**\n  - *\"make sure for the proper alignment of images as they are not visible correctly\"*\n  - *\"use actual matrix and determinant bracket for 3x3 matrix and other sizes also use brackets matrix of word file\"*\n\n---\n\n### 3. Work Accomplished\n- **Generated 4 Word Documents (`.docx`) & 4 Text Files (`.txt`):**\n  - `Set_A_Question_Paper.docx` & `Set_A_Question_Paper.txt`\n  - `Set_A_Marking_Scheme.docx` & `Set_A_Marking_Scheme.txt`\n  - `Set_B_Question_Paper.docx` & `Set_B_Question_Paper.txt`\n  - `Set_B_Marking_Scheme.docx` & `Set_B_Marking_Scheme.txt`\n- **Native Word OMML Equations for Matrices & Determinants:**\n  - Implemented OpenXML/OMML (`xmlns:m=\"http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/math\"`) elements:\n    - Matrices: `<m:d>` with delimiter `begChr=\"[\"` and `endChr=\"]\"` with `<m:m>` grid.\n    - Determinants: `<m:d>` with delimiter `begChr=\"|\"` and `endChr=\"|\"`.\n    - Implemented across all 3x3 matrices (Q6, Q32, Q33), 2x2 matrices (Q22), 3x1 column vectors (Q33), and 3x3 determinants (Q28) in both Set A & Set B question papers and marking schemes.\n- **Embedded High-Contrast 300 DPI Diagrams with Non-Clipping Paragraphs:**\n  - Set A & Set B Case Study 1: Relations & Functions (Set partition / Divisibility graph).\n  * Set A & Set B Case Study 2: Application of Derivatives (Cost curve $C(x)$ / Revenue curve $R(x)$).\n  * Set A & Set B Case Study 3: Integrals (Velocity-Time kinematic graphs).\n  * Set A & Set B Assertion-Reason: Function graphs ($y=|x-2|$, $y=-(x-3)^2+4$, $y=[x]$, $y=\\ln x$).\n- **Deleted Syllabus Audit & Replacement:**\n  - Removed all 5 occurrences of Tangents & Normals questions across Section A and Section B, replacing them with Rate of Change of Quantities, Maximum/Minimum values, and Marginal Revenue calculations.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Model Knowledge\n- **Word Picture Clipping Quirk in `python-docx`:**\n  - If a paragraph inherits a fixed line spacing (e.g. `pf.line_spacing = Pt(14)` from the `Normal` style), Word clips inline images to a height of 14 points (rendering them as thin, invisible strips).\n  - **Solution:** Any paragraph containing a picture must explicitly set `p.paragraph_format.line_spacing = None` and `p.paragraph_format.line_spacing_rule = WD_LINE_SPACING.SINGLE` with center alignment.\n- **Word File Locks on Windows:**\n  - If `Set_A_Question_Paper.docx` is opened by Word, writing to it will throw `PermissionError: [Errno 13]`. Running `powershell -Command \"Get-Process WINWORD -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | Stop-Process -Force\"` frees the handle before saving.\n- **Native OMML Equation Structure:**\n  - In `python-docx`, native equations are inserted via `paragraph._element.append(parse_xml(xml))` using the `<m:oMath>` namespace.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Files and Code\n\n#### Location of Generated Exam Package\nDirectory: `C:\\Users\\rajan\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\math_exam_2026\\`\n\n#### Files Generated / Modified:\n1. `C:\\Users\\rajan\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\math_exam_2026\\Set_A_Question_Paper.docx` (Word doc for Set A QP with OMML brackets & 300 DPI images)\n2. `C:\\Users\\rajan\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\math_exam_2026\\Set_A_Marking_Scheme.docx` (Word doc for Set A Marking Scheme with step marks & OMML matrices)\n3. `C:\\Users\\rajan\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\math_exam_2026\\Set_B_Question_Paper.docx` (Word doc for Set B QP with OMML brackets & 300 DPI images)\n4. `C:\\Users\\rajan\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\math_exam_2026\\Set_B_Marking_Scheme.docx` (Word doc for Set B Marking Scheme with step marks & OMML matrices)\n5. `C:\\Users\\rajan\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\math_exam_2026\\Set_A_Question_Paper.txt` (Text format of Set A QP)\n6. `C:\\Users\\rajan\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\math_exam_2026\\Set_A_Marking_Scheme.txt` (Text format of Set A MS)\n7. `C:\\Users\\rajan\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\math_exam_2026\\Set_B_Question_Paper.txt` (Text format of Set B QP)\n8. `C:\\Users\\rajan\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\math_exam_2026\\Set_B_Marking_Scheme.txt` (Text format of Set B MS)\n9. `C:\\Users\\rajan\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\math_exam_2026\\images\\` (Contains 10 PNG diagrams: `set_a_q19.png`, `set_a_q20.png`, `set_a_q36.png`, `set_a_q37.png`, `set_a_q38.png`, `set_b_q19.png`, `set_b_q20.png`, `set_b_q36.png`, `set_b_q37.png`, `set_b_q38.png`)\n\n#### Key Script Files:\n1. `C:\\Users\\rajan\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\b78a5d36-6586-4c94-a487-70da0c9f5362\\scratch\\build_full_exam_with_omml.py`: Master generation script