ions (9 points as per CBSE pattern)\\n- All 5 sections\\n\\nHere are ALL the questions:\\n\\n--- SECTION A (20 x 1 = 20 marks) ---\\n\\nQ1. Let R = {(1,1), (2,2), (3,3), (1,3), (3,1)} be a relation on A = {1, 2, 3}. Then R is:\\n(a) Reflexive only    (b) Symmetric only\\n(c) An equivalence relation    (d) Reflexive and symmetric only\\n\\nQ2. The number of all one-one functions from the set {1, 2, 3} to itself is:\\n(a) 3    (b) 6    (c) 9    (d) 27\\n\\nQ3. The principal value of cos⁻¹(-1/√2) is:\\n(a) π/4    (b) 3π/4    (c) -π/4    (d) 5π/4\\n\\nQ4. The range of the principal value branch of tan⁻¹x is:\\n(a) [-π/2, π/2]    (b) (-π/2, π/2)    (c) [0, π]    (d) (0, π)\\n\\nQ5. If A and B are square matrices of the same order, then (A + B)ᵀ equals:\\n(a) Aᵀ + Bᵀ    (b) Aᵀ - Bᵀ    (c) AᵀBᵀ    (d) BᵀAᵀ\\n\\nQ6. If the matrix\\n        | 0   a  -3 |\\nA =     | 2   0  -1 |\\n        | b   1   0 |\\nis a skew-symmetric matrix, then the value of a + b is:\\n(a) 1    (b) -1    (c) 5    (d) -5\\n\\nQ7. A matrix A = [aᵢⱼ]₃ₓ₃ is a diagonal matrix if:\\n(a) aᵢⱼ = 0 for all i, j    (b) aᵢⱼ = 0 for i ≠ j\\n(c) aᵢⱼ = 0 for i = j    (d) aᵢⱼ ≠ 0 for all i, j\\n\\nQ8. If A is a 3 x 3 matrix with |A| = -2, then |3A| equals:\\n(a) -6    (b) -54    (c) 54    (d) -18\\n\\nQ9. The area of the triangle with vertices (1, 0), (6, 0) and (4, 3), found using determinants, is:\\n(a) 15 sq units    (b) 15/2 sq units    (c) 7 sq units    (d) 12 sq units\\n\\nQ10. If y = sin(3x), then dy/dx is:\\n(a) cos(3x)    (b) 3cos(3x)    (c) -3cos(3x)    (d) 3sin(3x)\\n\\nQ11. The function f(x) = x³ is:\\n(a) Continuous but not differentiable at x = 0\\n(b) Differentiable but not continuous at x = 0\\n(c) Both continuous and differentiable everywhere on R\\n(d) Neither continuous nor differentiable at x = 0\\n\\nQ12. The value of k for which the function f(x) = kx², x ≤ 2 and f(x) = 3, x > 2, is continuous at x = 2, is:\\n(a) 3/4    (b) 4/3    (c) 3    (d) 4\\n\\nQ13. The rate of change of the volume V = (4